  "generated_text": "Given the functional equation \\( b^2 f(a) = a^2 f(b) \\), we need to find \\( \\frac{f(5) - f(1)}{f(2)} \\).\n\nFirst, let's substitute \\( a = 1 \\) and \\( b = 2 \\) into the functional equation:\n\\[\n2^2 f(1) = 1^2 f(2)\n\\]\n\\[\n4 f(1) = f(2)\n\\]\n\nNext, let's substitute \\( a = 5 \\) and \\( b = 2 \\) into the functional equation:\n\\[\n2^2 f(5) = 5^2 f(2)\n\\]\n\\[\n4 f(5) = 25 f(2)\n\\]\n\\[\nf(5) = \\frac{25}{4} f(2)\n\\]\n\nWe need to find \\( \\frac{f(5) - f(1)}{f(2)} \\):\n\\[\n\\frac{f(5) - f(1)}{f(2)} = 4\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{4}\n\\]",
  "grade": {
    "error": null,
    "extracted_answer": "[4, '4']",
    "gold_answer": "Setting $a = 5$ and $b = 2,$ we get\n\\[4f(5) = 25f(2),\\]so $\\frac{f(5)}{f(2)} = \\frac{25}{4}.$\n\nSetting $a = 1$ and $b = 2,$ we get\n\\[4f(1) = f(2),\\]so $\\frac{f(1)}{f(2)} = \\frac{1}{4}.$  Hence,\n\\[\\frac{f(5) - f(1)}{f(2)} = \\frac{25}{4} - \\frac{1}{4} = \\boxed{6}.\\]",
    "is_correct": false
  },
